From: Chu Qinghao <6337103+qinghao1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 2 Nov 2026 00:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 7/9] bridge: ignore window focus in headless IsPlaying

Headless has no OS window, so SDL_GetKeyboardFocus() never reports the
playfield window and IsPlaying() stays false forever: UpdatePhysics and
the animated-parts update never run while script and PinMAME (never
focus-gated) work fine. Skip the focus check when VPX_HEADLESS_BRIDGE
is set; nothing else can auto-pause a focusless session.

Target: vpinball/vpinball@64a480a96d1b972711fbb8eea014654c779b1e23

--- a/src/core/player.h
+++ b/src/core/player.h
@@ -85,7 +85,12 @@ public:
    string GetPerfInfo();
 
    void SetPlayState(const bool isPlaying, const uint32_t delayBeforePauseMs = 0); // Allow to play/pause during UI interaction or to perform timed simulation steps (still needs the player window to be focused).
+#ifdef VPX_HEADLESS_BRIDGE
+   // Headless sessions have no keyboard focus; gate play state on intent only.
+   bool IsPlaying(const bool applyWndFocus = true) const { (void)applyWndFocus; return (m_playMode == PlayMode::CaptureAttract) || (m_wantsToPlay && !IsEditorMode()); }
+#else
    bool IsPlaying(const bool applyWndFocus = true) const { return (m_playMode == PlayMode::CaptureAttract) || (m_wantsToPlay && (applyWndFocus ? m_playfieldWnd->IsFocused() : true) && !IsEditorMode()); }
+#endif
    void OnFocusChanged(); // On focus lost, pause player and show mouse cursor
 
    uint32_t m_pauseTimeTarget = 0;
